p("At the operating point selected by the false-alarm budget, FTT-IDS has the highest mean F1 (93.65%) and the lowest FPR (4.44%) among the six models of Table 3. This comparison must be read with care, because the same validation budget places the models at different points of their test ROC curves: the realised test FPR ranges from 4.4% (FTT-IDS) to 6.5% (FT-Transformer). Table 4 therefore compares the models at matched test false-alarm rates. At 1% test FPR, XGBoost detects 86.2% of attacks and FTT-IDS 85.6%; the difference is smaller than the seed-to-seed standard deviation of FTT-IDS (1.1 points). FTT-IDS is ahead of RF (84.2%) and FT-Transformer (84.1%) and clearly ahead of the MLP and the 1D-CNN. At 5% FPR, the four strongest models lie within 0.5 points of each other, and the partial ROC-AUC ranks XGBoost and FTT-IDS first and practically equal (0.9501 and 0.9496).")
