p("Table 5 gives the paired tests at the validation-selected thresholds. At τ_{FPR}(1%), FTT-IDS has a higher F1 than the MLP (+0.85 points), the 1D-CNN (+0.75), FT-Transformer (+0.34) and the single-token control (+2.72); it is marginally ahead of RF (+0.13, 95% CI [+0.02, +0.23]) and statistically indistinguishable from XGBoost (+0.06, [−0.04, +0.16]). At the F1-optimal threshold τ_{F1}, RF and XGBoost hold a small advantage (−0.20 and −0.42 points). In view of Table 4, the small advantage over RF at τ_{FPR}(1%) partly reflects the more conservative operating point that the budget assigns to FTT-IDS, not better ranking alone. Taken together, the feature-token Transformer is competitive with, but not superior to, well-tuned gradient-boosted trees, in agreement with tabular-learning benchmarks {grinsztajn,shwartz}.")
