p("Table 6 shows the corresponding results on TON_IoT. Once duplicates and host identifiers are removed, the task remains nearly separable for all models (F1 ≥ 99.4%, ROC-AUC ≥ 0.998). The tree ensembles lead (XGBoost F1 99.77%, FPR 0.76%), and FTT-IDS (99.50%, 1.58%) is significantly below RF and XGBoost (ΔF1 −0.33 and −0.36 points at τ_{FPR}(1%); median McNemar *p* < 10^{−17}, significant for all seeds) and on par with the neural baselines. With all models above 99.4% F1, this dataset has little power to separate methods; it serves mainly as a second, IoT-oriented testbed on which the conclusions about decision rules and explanations can be checked.")
